+# "backfield gap" denial spot when it has an objective trip that needs no
+# fight — an uncontrolled, non-home objective with no enemy OC one move away,
+# that a friendly unit already holds or is going to — scoring at least
+# SCREEN_VS_OBJECTIVE_MIN_GAIN above the screen, and that trip itself passes
+# the TOO-LATE / RACE-SKIP / LONE-TRIP / FAR-TRIP gates and is not a lost race.
+# It joins that objective instead; the gap is consumed (as if screened), so
+# every other unit keeps its base assignment. At most one such switch per
+# movement plan; a unit standing on an objective keeps its base gap screen;
+# home-objective deep-strike denial is untouched. s7467 r1 P2 Gretchin:
+# Advancing onto obj_nml_2 measured +3.64 [1.82, 5.46] over 36 seeds.
+# Fires only when the enemy has units in reserve. 0 = base.
+const FIX_SCREEN_VS_OBJECTIVE: float = 1.0
+# SCREEN-VS-OBJ: the released trip must score at least this much above the
+# gap screen it replaces.
+const SCREEN_VS_OBJECTIVE_MIN_GAIN: float = 8.0
 const CHARGE_SHORT_6IN_MULT: float = 1.2  # charge: needs 6" or less (reliability multiplier)
 const CHARGE_TARGET_ON_OBJ_MULT: float = 1.5  # charge: target is standing on an objective
